- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget Speech 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_Speech_english_2022_23.pdf","claim":"Sharif presented the first budget of a coalition government and said the government chose difficult reforms rather than early elections because it wanted to restore the economy and move the country back on track.","locator":"pp. 1-2, lines 6-18 and 38-51","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech with the prime minister's framing of the government's governing choice and priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: this is Sharif's own budget speech as prime minister.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is self-justifying and not an independent assessment of success.","It states intent and strategic choice more clearly than implementation results."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3","8B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget Speech 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_Speech_english_2022_23.pdf","claim":"Sharif said the government would prioritize economic stability, support middle and poor households, raise domestic production and agriculture, and improve exports and ease of doing business.","locator":"pp. 3-5, lines 63-84 and 87-92","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech with a clear policy program and target groups.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the statement is Sharif's own policy framing in office.","contrary_evidence":["This is a declared program, not proof of delivery.","The speech also blames the predecessor government, so some of the framing is adversarial."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.7"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget Speech 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_Speech_english_2022_23.pdf","claim":"The government said it had implemented a Rs2,000 monthly cash transfer for families with income below Rs40,000 from June 2022 and would add about 60 million more people to BISP.","locator":"pp. 8-9, lines 157-167","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech with a specific cash-transfer policy, start date, and scale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Sharif as prime minister announcing and incorporating the measure into the coalition budget.","contrary_evidence":["The claim is programmatic and self-reported, not an independent disbursement audit.","It reflects relief and cushioning more than broad productivity reform."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget in Brief 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_in_Brief_English.pdf","claim":"The budget raised BISP funding from Rs250 billion to Rs364 billion, projected access for nine million families under Kafalat, expanded educational scholarships to 10 million students, extended Nashonuma nutrition coverage, and increased Pakistan Bait-ul-Mal support for the poor.","locator":"pp. 15-17, lines 313-333","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget summary with explicit allocations and beneficiary targets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Shared but meaningful: this is the federal budget under Sharif's premiership, though delivery would depend on implementing agencies.","contrary_evidence":["Allocated amounts and target counts do not prove actual completion in 2022.","These are social-protection commitments inside a fiscally stressed budget."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Performance Based Budget FY 2022-23 to 2024-25","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Performance_Based_Budget_FY_2022_23_to_2024_25.pdf","claim":"The budget framework defined BISP's goal as a nationwide safety net with effective and transparent targeting and delivery mechanisms, and tied it to concrete outputs including unconditional cash transfers, emergency cash transfers, Waseela-e-Taleem, NSER, and Nashonuma.","locator":"p. 192-193, lines 18329-18339 and 18354-18371","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary performance-budget document that links funding to goals and named delivery mechanisms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Shared attribution: this is a federal performance-budget architecture under Sharif's government, not a personal PM audit of each program arm.","contrary_evidence":["This shows institutional design more than realized outcomes.","Performance targets can be aspirational rather than achieved."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget in Brief 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_in_Brief_English.pdf","claim":"The Public Sector Development Programme was presented as the main instrument for improving socio-economic conditions and achieving government targets, with the 2022-23 budget laying out PSDP size and special packages and relief.","locator":"pp. 55-56, lines 2181-2191 and 2198-2207","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget document explicitly linking PSDP to government targets and social-economic goals.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the PSDP framework is a government choice under Sharif, though execution would sit with multiple ministries and provinces.","contrary_evidence":["The document explains planning, not completed implementation.","Large development allocations do not ensure project delivery under crisis conditions."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan to cut expenditures, development funds to revive IMF programme","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-20","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/pakistan-to-cut-expenditures-development-funds-to-revive-imf-programme-2806777","claim":"Finance Minister Miftah Ismail said Pakistan would cut expenditures and development funds and do belt tightening to revive the IMF programme.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a concrete fiscal-adaptation decision is strong and specific, even when syndicated through a secondary site.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but real: this reflects the Sharif government's economic response through its finance minister.","contrary_evidence":["Cutting development funds can also indicate weakness or austerity under duress.","The statement is about intended fiscal correction, not guaranteed recovery."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9"]}
